In the `Main` method, we create an instance of the `PdfExtractor` class with the path to the PDF file. We then call the `GetImagesFromPage` and `GetHyperlinksFromPage` methods to extract images and hyperlinks from page 1.

Please note that this is a simple example and may not work for complex PDFs. Also, the `GetImages` method will return the image data in a format suitable for use with libraries like System.Drawing, but the `GetHyperlinksFromPage` method will return the URI as a string.

Also, remember to add the UglyToad.PdfPig namespace to your using directives.

Please ensure that the path to the PDF file and the page number in the `Main` method are correct. If the PDF file is password protected, you may need to open the document using a `PdfDocumentFactory` and providing the password.

