Assistant:  Here is a basic implementation of a C# class that uses the UglyToad.PdfPig library to extract images and hyperlinks from a PDF document.

```csharp
using UglyToad.PdfPig;
using UglyToad.PdfPig.Content;
using UglyToad.PdfPig.Util;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.IO;
using System.Linq;

public class PdfProcessor
{
    private string _filePath;

    public PdfProcessor(string filePath)
    {
        _filePath = filePath;
    }

    public IEnumerable<XObjectImage> GetImagesFromPage(int pageNumber)
    {
        using (var pdfDocument = PdfDocument.Open(_filePath))
        {
            var page = pdfDocument.GetPage(pageNumber);
            var images = new List<XObjectImage>();

            if (page.ExperimentalAccess.TryGetImages(out var pageImages))
            {
                foreach (var image in pageImages)
                {
                    images.Add(image);
                }
            }

            return images;
        }
    }

    public IEnumerable<ILocation> GetHyperlinksFromPage(int pageNumber)
    {
        using (var pdfDocument = PdfDocument.Open(_filePath))
        {
            var page = pdfDocument.GetPage(pageNumber);
            var hyperlinks = new List<ILocation>();

            var annotations = page.ExperimentalAccess.GetAnnotations();
            foreach (var annotation in annotations)
            {
                if (annotation.AnnotationType == AnnotationType.Link)
                {
                    hyperlinks.Add(annotation.Location);
                }
            }

            return hyperlinks;
        }
    }
}
```

In this class, the constructor takes a file path as a parameter to the PDF document. The `GetImagesFromPage` method extracts all images from a specified page and returns them as a collection of `XObjectImage` objects. The `GetHyperlinksFromPage` method extracts all hyperlinks from a specified page and returns them as a collection of `ILocation` objects.

To use this class, create an instance of `PdfProcessor` and call the desired method:

```csharp
var processor = new PdfProcessor(@"C:\Users\Kris\test.pdf");
var images = processor.GetImagesFromPage(1);
var hyperlinks = processor.GetHyperlinksFromPage(1);
```

Note: The `GetImagesFromPage` method returns the images in the page as `XObjectImage` objects, which contain the raw image data and other information about the image. If you want to save the images to a file, you'll need to process them further.

The `GetHyperlinksFromPage` method returns the hyperlinks in the page as `ILocation` objects, which contain information about the location and size of the link. If you want to use the hyperlinks, you'll need to process them further.

The UglyToad.PdfPig library is open-source and available on GitHub. You can find it here: https://github.com/UglyToad/PdfPig.

