using iText.Kernel.Pdf;
using iText.Kernel.Utils;
using System.Collections.Generic;

public class PdfProcessor
{
    public byte[] MergePdfFiles(List<string> filePaths)
    {
        using (var pdfOutput = new PdfDocument(new PdfWriter("merged.pdf")))
        {
            foreach (string filePath in filePaths)
            {
                using (var pdfSource = new PdfDocument(new PdfReader(filePath)))
                {
                    var pages = PdfDocumentUtil.GetAllPages(pdfSource, pdfOutput);
                    foreach (var page in pages)
                    {
                        pdfOutput.AddPage(page);
                    }
                }
            }

            byte[] bytes = new byte[0];
            using (var ms = new MemoryStream())
            {
                pdfOutput.Close();

                bytes = File.ReadAllBytes("merged.pdf");
                File.Delete("merged.pdf");
            }

            return bytes;
        }
    }
}
```

In this class, the `MergePdfFiles` method takes a list of PDF file paths and merges them into a single PDF document. It returns a byte array that represents the merged PDF file.

The `PdfMerger` class from the iText library is used to merge the PDF files. The `PdfWriter` class is used to write the merged PDF document to a file, and the `PdfDocument` class is used to read the PDF files. The `PdfDocumentUtil.GetAllPages` method is used to get all pages from the source PDF document and add them to the output PDF document.

Please note that iText library is not available via NuGet, so you'll need to download it from the official iText website and add it as a reference to your project. Also, this code doesn't handle exceptions, you might want to add try-catch blocks around the code to handle potential exceptions.

