Assistant:  Here's an example of how you can extract images and hyperlinks from a PDF page. The `GetImagesFromPage` method extracts images and the `GetHyperlinksFromPage` method extracts hyperlinks.

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.IO;
using UglyToad.PdfPig;
using UglyToad.PdfPig.Content;
using UglyToad.PdfPig.Core;

public class PdfExtractor
{
    public static List<byte[]> GetImagesFromPage(string filePath, int pageNumber)
    {
        List<byte[]> images = new List<byte[]>();

        using (PdfDocument document = PdfDocument.Open(filePath))
        {
            PdfPage page = document.GetPage(pageNumber);

            foreach (var image in page.GetImages())
            {
                byte[] imageData = image.Data;
                images.Add(imageData);
            }
        }

        return images;
    }

    public static List<string> GetHyperlinksFromPage(string filePath, int pageNumber)
    {
        List<string> hyperlinks = new List<string>();

        using (PdfDocument document = PdfDocument.Open(filePath))
        {
            PdfPage page = document.GetPage(pageNumber);

            foreach (var annotation in page.Annotations)
            {
                if (annotation is PdfLinkAnnotation linkAnnotation)
                {
                    string hyperlink = linkAnnotation.Uri;
                    hyperlinks.Add(hyperlink);
                }
            }
        }

        return hyperlinks;
    }
}
```

In this example, the `GetImagesFromPage` method gets all the images from a specific page in the PDF document. The `GetHyperlinksFromPage` method gets all the hyperlinks from a specific page in the PDF document.

Please note that the `PdfImage` class in UglyToad.PdfPig does not currently support image extraction. You may need to use another library or implement image extraction yourself. For hyperlinks, `PdfLinkAnnotation` class is used to get the hyperlinks from the page.

To extract images, you might have to use another library that supports extracting images from PDFs, such as `iTextSharp`, `PdfiumLibrary`, etc. For hyperlinks, UglyToad.PdfPig is good enough for extracting hyperlinks.

