User: Implement a C# class that merges C:\Users\Kris\test.pdf with one or more additional PDF files into a single document using PdfMerger. Provide a method MergePdfFiles that accepts file paths and outputs a byte array.
Assistant:   To merge multiple PDF files into a single document using PdfPig library in C#, follow the steps below:

First, let's create a new class `PdfMerger`:

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using UglyToad.PdfPig;

namespace PdfPigDemo
{
    public class PdfMerger
    {
        public byte[] MergePdfFiles(params string[] filePaths)
        {
            using (var masterDocument = new PdfDocument())
            {
                masterDocument.Open();

                // Merge each additional PDF file into the master document
                foreach (var filePath in filePaths)
                {
                    using (var slaveDocument = new PdfDocument(filePath))
                    {
                        masterDocument.Merge(slaveDocument);
                        slaveDocument.Close();
                    }
                }

                // Save the merged document as a byte array
                using (var ms = new MemoryStream())
                {
                    masterDocument.Save(ms, new PdfSaveOptions());
                    return ms.ToArray();
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The `MergePdfFiles` method accepts a variable number of file paths as arguments and merges them into a single document. The resulting merged document is then saved as a byte array.

To use the `PdfMerger` class, create an instance and call the `MergePdfFiles` method:

```csharp
class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        var pdfMerger = new PdfMerger();
        var mergedPdfAsByteArray = pdfMerger.MergePdfFiles("C:/Users/Kris/test.pdf", "C:/Users/Kris/anotherfile.pdf");

        // Save the merged PDF to a file
        File.WriteAllBytes("merged.pdf", mergedPdfAsByteArray);
        Console.WriteLine("Merged PDF saved.");
    }
}
```

