Assistant:  I'd be happy to help you write a C# class that extracts words from a PDF file using NearestNeighbourWordExtractor and groups them by page number. However, it's important to note that NearestNeighbourWordExtractor is not a built-in class in .NET or the PdfPig library. You would need to use an external library like Tesseract OCR for text recognition to achieve this functionality. Here's an example of how you might structure your class:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using Tesseract;
using UglyToad.PdfPig;

namespace PdfWordExtractor
{
    public class PdfWordExtractor
    {
        public Dictionary<int, Dictionary<string, int>> ExtractWordsByPage(string filePath)
        {
            using (PdfDocument pdfDocument = PdfDocument.Load(filePath))
            {
                var wordsByPage = new Dictionary<int, Dictionary<string, int>>();

                for (int pageNumber = 0; pageNumber < pdfDocument.PageCount; pageNumber++)
                {
                    wordsByPage[pageNumber + 1] = new Dictionary<string, int>();

                    using (ITesseract engine = new TesseractEngine())
                    {
                        engine.Init(@"C:\path\to\tesseract\tessdata", "eng");

                        PdfPage pdfPage = pdfDocument[pageNumber];
                        using (var img = new PdfImage(pdfPage))
                        {
                            using (var page = engine.CreatePageFromImage(img))
                            {
                                var words = engine.Process(page).GetWords();

                                foreach (var word in words)
                                {
                                    wordsByPage[pageNumber + 1].Add(word.Text, word.Position.Left + word.Position.Top);
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        engine.Dispose();
                    }
                }

                return wordsByPage;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

In the code above, we're using the Tesseract OCR library to extract text from the PDF pages. We're assuming that the Tesseract library is installed in the specified path `C:\path\to\tesseract\tessdata`. If you have Tesseract installed elsewhere, update the path accordingly.

The `ExtractWordsByPage` method loads the PDF document, initializes the Tesseract engine, iterates through each page, extracts words using Tesseract, and stores the words and their positions in a dictionary. The words and their positions are then added to the outer dictionary, which groups the words by page number.

To use the class, simply instantiate it and call the `ExtractWordsByPage` method:

```csharp
