Assistant:  In this example, I will create a simple C# class called `PdfMerger` and demonstrate how to merge multiple PDF files into a single document using iTextSharp. The `MergePdfFiles` method accepts an array of file paths as input and returns the merged PDF file as a byte array.

```csharp
using iText.Kernel.Pdf;
using iText.Layout;
using iText.Layout.Element;
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Linq;

public class PdfMerger
{
    public byte[] MergePdfFiles(string[] filePaths, string outputPath)
    {
        using (var ms = new MemoryStream())
        {
            using (var writer = new PdfWriter(ms))
            {
                using (var pdfDocument = new PdfDocument(writer))
                {
                    foreach (var filePath in filePaths)
                    {
                        using (var reader = new PdfReader(filePath))
                        {
                            for (int pageNumber = 1; pageNumber <= reader.NumberOfPages; pageNumber++)
                            {
                                var page = pdfDocument.AddNewPage(reader.GetPageSize(pageNumber));
                                var contentByte = page.CreateContent();
                                contentByte.AddTemplate(reader.GetPageTemplate(pageNumber));
                            }
                            reader.Close();
                        }
                    }

                    pdfDocument.Close();
                }

                ms.Seek(0, SeekOrigin.Begin);
                byte[] mergedPdfBytes = ms.ToArray();
                ms.Close();

                File.WriteAllBytes(outputPath, mergedPdfBytes);

                return mergedPdfBytes;
            }
        }
    }
}
```

This `PdfMerger` class includes a `MergePdfFiles` method that accepts an array of file paths and a single output path as input. The method uses a `MemoryStream` to write the merged PDF data to a byte array. The merged PDF document is then saved to the specified output path using the `File.WriteAllBytes` method.

To test the class, you can create a new instance of the `PdfMerger` class and call the `MergePdfFiles` method:

