Assistant:  To merge multiple PDF files into a single document using the `PdfPig` library, you can create a class called `PdfMerger`. This class will include a method called `MergePdfFiles` that accepts a list of file paths and returns a byte array representing the merged PDF document.

First, ensure you have the `UglyToad.PdfPig` package installed via NuGet:

```bash
dotnet add package UglyToad.PdfPig
```

Now, create the `PdfMerger` class:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.IO;
using UglyToad.PdfPig;
using UglyToad.PdfPig.Writer;

public class PdfMerger
{
    public byte[] MergePdfFiles(List<string> filePaths)
    {
        if (filePaths == null || filePaths.Count == 0)
        {
            throw new ArgumentException("File paths cannot be null or empty.");
        }

        using (MemoryStream mergedStream = new MemoryStream())
        {
            using (PdfDocumentBuilder documentBuilder = PdfDocumentBuilder.Create(mergedStream))
            {
                foreach (string filePath in filePaths)
                {
                    using (PdfDocument document = PdfDocument.Open(filePath))
                    {
                        foreach (Page page in document.GetPages())
                        {
                            documentBuilder.AddPage(page);
                        }
                    }
                }
                documentBuilder.Save();
            }

            return mergedStream.ToArray();
        }
    }
}
```

### Usage Example

You can use the `PdfMerger` class to merge multiple PDF files into a single document and get the merged PDF as a byte array.

```csharp
class Program
{
    static void Main()
    {
        List<string> filePaths = new List<string>
        {
            @"C:\Users\Kris\test.pdf",
            @"C:\Users\Kris\additional.pdf",
            // Add more file paths as needed
        };

        PdfMerger merger = new PdfMerger();
        byte[] mergedPdf = merger.MergePdfFiles(filePaths);

        // Save the merged PDF to a file
        string outputFilePath = @"C:\Users\Kris\merged.pdf";
        File.WriteAllBytes(outputFilePath, mergedPdf);
        Console.WriteLine($"Merged PDF saved to {outputFilePath}");
    }
}
```

### Explanation

1. **PdfMerger Class**:
   - `MergePdfFiles`: This method accepts a list of file paths, opens each PDF file, and adds its pages to a new `PdfDocumentBuilder`. It then saves the merged document to a `MemoryStream` and returns the byte array representing the merged PDF.

2. **Usage Example**:
   - The `Main` method demonstrates how to use the `PdfMerger` class to merge multiple PDF files into a single document and save the merged PDF to a file.

This solution should help you merge multiple PDF files into a single document using C# and the `PdfPig` library.
